    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Air temperature and relative humidity were measured in the upper third of the canopy in each plot (Vaisala HMP35C and HMP45C; Helsinki, Finland). Saturated vapor pressure and vapor pressure deficit were calculated using the air temperature and relative humidity measurements. Net radiation was measured above the canopy using Fritschen\u2010type net radiometers (Q7, REBS, Seattle, WA, USA) and CNR1 net radiometers (Kipp & Zonen, Delft, the Netherlands). Photosynthetically active radiation was measured with Q190 sensors (LiCor, Lincoln, Nebraska, USA). Tipping buckets (TE525M; Texas Electronics, Dallas, TX, USA) were installed at the top of the center tower to measure precipitation. Soil temperature was measured with thermistors (334-NTC102-RC; Xicon Passive Components) buried at 10 cm depth in each plot. Volumetric soil water content of the upper 30 cm soil layer was measured with time-domain reflectometry probes (CS615 or CS616L; Campbell Scientific, Logan, UT, USA) at four locations in plots 1-6 since 1997 and at eight locations (5-10 cm depth and 25-30 cm depth; (ThetaProbe ML1x or ML2x; Delta\u2010T Devices, Cambridge, UK) in plots 7-8 since 2001. Soil moisture was rescaled with the hygroscopic minimum (0.125 m3 m-3) and the measured porosity (0.540 m3 m-3) at the site. All sensors were sampled every 30 seconds and 30\u2010minute averages were logged (CR21X or CR23X; Campbell Scientific, Logan, UT, USA)."
    ],
